One file per arm, sourced by docker/flavour-setup.sh inside the image.

  RCC_SUITES        Debian suites the arm builds on, "testing stable" or one of them
  RCC_ARCH          restrict to one architecture, empty = any
  RCC_SYSDEPS       apt packages
  RCC_SYSDEB_URLS   .deb files fetched by URL (for packages no longer in the suite)
  RCC_APT_SOURCE    extra apt source in deb822 form, '|' between lines
  RCC_APT_KEY       signing key for that source, a file in this directory
  RCC_APT_PIN       apt preferences content, applied before RCC_SYSDEB_URLS
  RCC_APT_HOLD      packages to apt-mark hold after install
  RCC_APT_REMOVE    packages to remove before RCC_SYSDEB_URLS, if installed
  RCC_RCONF_FLAGS   flags passed through build-R to Rconf
  RCC_LDFLAGS       appended to the configure line
  RCC_SETUP_SCRIPT  script in this directory, run after the packages are installed
  RCC_CHECK_ENV     NAME=value settings exported while checking, '|' between them
  RCC_DESC          one-line description, written to /etc/rcheck/flavour.txt

flavour-setup.sh sets RCC_SUITE to testing or stable, whichever the image is
built on, and RCC_CODENAME to the release's name, before it reads the file.
An arm whose packages differ between the two tests RCC_SUITE, as blis.env
does. The workflows and the demo scripts also read the file outside an image,
where neither is set, so give both a default.

An arm can also export variables that Rconf reads from the environment, as
clang23.env does with CXX_STDLIB.
